Description: Fits semiparametric joint models for longitudinal electronic health record (EHR) data that addresses two-stage hierarchical missingness mechanism. The first stage is the visiting process, and the second stage is the observation process. The core GIVEHR estimator uses a three-stage procedure: partial likelihood with log-normal frailty for visit intensity, probit regression with shared latent factor-linked random effects for observation, and weighted least squares with risk-set centering for the ouctome. These three stages are connected through a shared latent factor that induces dependence across all three processes. Two extensions handal temporal dependence in the observation process: Gauss-Hermite quadrature with online filtering (GIVEHR_GH) and Ornstein-Uhlenbeck pairwise composite likelihood (GIVEHR_OU_PCL). A data simulator and implementations of common benchmark methods (linear midex models, multiple imputation, and others) are included for comparative studies. Detailed methods are described in Yang, Shi, and Mukherjee (2026) <https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2602.15374>.
